"classes.conf (5)  - class configuration file for cups\n"
"backend (1)       - cups backend transmission interfaces\n"
"filter (1)        - cups file conversion filter interfaces\n"
"cups-polld (8)    - cups printer polling daemon\n"
"mime.types (5)    - mime type description file for cups\n"
"cupsd (8)         - common unix printing system daemon\n"
"lpadmin (8)       - configure cups printers and classes\n"
"cupsd.conf (5)    - server configuration file for cups\n"
"mime.convs (5)    - mime type conversion file for cups\n"
"printers.conf (5) - printer configuration file for cups\n"
"mime.convs (5)    - mime type conversion file for cups\n"
"cups-polld (8)    - cups printer polling daemon\n"
"lpstat (1)        - print cups status information\n"
"backend (1)       - cups backend transmission interfaces\n"
"mime.types (5)    - mime type description file for cups\n"
"cupsd (8)         - common unix printing system daemon\n"
"lpadmin (8)       - configure cups printers and classes\n"
"printers.conf (5) - printer configuration file for cups\n"
"cupsd.conf (5)    - server configuration file for cups\n"
"filter (1)        - cups file conversion filter interfaces\n"
"</computeroutput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: cupsoptions.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Outside &kdeprint;: Hints &amp; Tips Tricks with &CUPS; on the Commandline"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: cupsoptions.docbook:84
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here are a few examples of options that are presently only available if you "
"use the commandline."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: cupsoptions.docbook:88
#, no-c-format
msgid "Allowing or denying printer access for certain users"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: cupsoptions.docbook:90
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When installing (or modifying) a printer through the command line, you can "
"either deny or allow the usage of that printer to certain users:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: cupsoptions.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput><command>lpadmin</command> <option>-p</"
"option><parameter>HeidelbergDigimaster9110</parameter> <option>-v</option> "
"<parameter>lpd:/10.160.16.99/mqueue</parameter> <option>-u</option> "
"<parameter>allow:kurt,sylvi,hansjoerg</parameter> <option>-E</option> "
"<option>-P</option> <parameter>/home/kurt/PPDs/DVHV.ppd</parameter></"
"userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: cupsoptions.docbook:96
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"will allow the usage of this (believe me: very nice and also very "
"professional) printer to only the three mentioned users and at the same time "
"deny it to all others. If another user wants to print on the DigiMaster via "
"this &CUPS; server, he will receive an error message along the lines "
"<errortype>client-error-not-possible</errortype>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: cupsoptions.docbook:102
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput><command>lpadmin</command> <option>-p</option> "
"<parameter>HeidelbergDigimaster9110</parameter> <option>-v</option> "
"<parameter>lpd:/10.160.16.99/mqueue</parameter> <option>-u</option> "
"<parameter>deny:tackat,boss,waba</parameter> <option>-E</option> <option>-P</"
"option> <parameter>/home/kurt/PPDs/DVHV.ppd</parameter></userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: cupsoptions.docbook:104
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"will deny the usage of this same printer to the three mentioned users and at "
"the same time allow it to all others. If <quote>denied</quote> user wants to "
"print on the DigiMaster via this &CUPS; server, he will receive an error "
"message along the lines <errortype>client-error-not-possible</errortype>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: cupsoptions.docbook:111
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Only one of the two options may be used at one time; at present there is no "
"support to have a similar option in a per-group based way. This will be "
"implemented in the future."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: cupsoptions.docbook:118
#, no-c-format
msgid "Imposing Quotas for certain printers"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: cupsoptions.docbook:120
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Sometimes you want to impose quotas for certain printers. With quotas you "
"can set upper limits for the number of pages or the amount of data to be "
"printed over a certain period to a certain printer."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: cupsoptions.docbook:124
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Quotas can be set with the <option>-o</option> option when installing a "
"printer with the <command>lpadmin</command> command, or afterwards for an "
"already existing printer. Following are some guidelines (which are missing "
"at the time of writing in the, official &CUPS; documentation):"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: cupsoptions.docbook:132
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With &CUPS; you may have pagecount- and filesize-based quotas for individual "
"printers."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: cupsoptions.docbook:137
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Quotas are calculated for each user individually (so a single set of limits "
"applies to all users for the printer concerned)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: cupsoptions.docbook:142
#, no-c-format
msgid "Quotas include banner pages (if those are used)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: cupsoptions.docbook:146
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This means: you can limit every user to 20 pages per day on an expensive "
"printer, but you cannot limit every user except <systemitem class=\"username"
"\">Kurt</systemitem> or <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: cupsoptions.docbook:153
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are <option>job-k-limit</option>, <option>job-page-limit</option>, and "
"<option>job-quota-period</option> options to give when setting up a printer."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: cupsoptions.docbook:159
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<option>job-quota-period</option> sets a time interval for quota computing "
"(intervals are determined in seconds; so a day is 60x60x24=86.400, a week is "
"60x60x24x7=604,800, and a month is 60x60x24x30=2.592.000 seconds.)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: cupsoptions.docbook:166
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For quotas to be enforced, the time-period <emphasis>plus</emphasis> at "
"least one job-limit must be set to non-zero."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: cupsoptions.docbook:172
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The default value of 0 for <option>job-k-limit</option> specifies that there "
"is no limit."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: cupsoptions.docbook:177
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The default value of 0 for <option>job-page-limit</option> specifies that "
"there is no limit."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: cupsoptions.docbook:182
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The default value of 0 for <option>job-quota-period</option> specifies that "
"the limits apply to all jobs that have been printed by a user that are still "
"known to the system."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: cupsoptions.docbook:189
#, no-c-format
msgid "Working Examples:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: cupsoptions.docbook:191
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Working, as both, time-period <emphasis>plus</emphasis> one or both job-"
"limits are defined"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: cupsoptions.docbook:194
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput><command>lpadmin</command> <option>-p</option> "
"<parameter>danka_infotec_4850</parameter> <option>-o</option> <parameter>job-"
"quota-period=604800</parameter> <option>-o</option> <parameter>job-k-"
"limit=1024</parameter></userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: cupsoptions.docbook:196
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This sets a limit of a file size of 1 MB (in total) for each user of "
"existing printer <systemitem class=\"resource\">danka_infotec_4850</"
"systemitem> during one week."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: cupsoptions.docbook:200
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput><command>lpadmin</command> <option>p</option> "
"<parameter>danka_infotec_4105</parameter> <option>-o</option> <parameter>job-"
"quota-period=604800</parameter> <option>-o</option> <parameter>job-page-"
"limit=100</parameter></userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: cupsoptions.docbook:202
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This sets a limit of 100 pages (in total) for each user of existing printer "
"<systemitem class=\"resource\">danka_infotec_4105</systemitem> during one "
"week."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: cupsoptions.docbook:206
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput><command>lpadmin</command> <option>-p</option> "
"<parameter>danka_infotec_P450</parameter> <option>-o</option> <parameter>job-"
"quota-period=604800</parameter> <option>-o</option> <parameter>job-k-"
"limit=1024</parameter> <option>-o</option> <parameter>job-page-limit=100</"
"parameter></userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: cupsoptions.docbook:208
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This sets a combined limit of 1 MB (in total) and 100 pages (in total) for "
"each user of existing printer <systemitem class=\"resource"
"\">danka_infotec_P450</systemitem> during one week. Whichever limit is "
"reached first will take effect."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: cupsoptions.docbook:216
#, no-c-format
msgid "Not working examples"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: cupsoptions.docbook:218
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<emphasis>NOT</emphasis> working, as only <emphasis>one</emphasis>, time-"
"period <emphasis>or</emphasis> job-limit is defined)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: cupsoptions.docbook:222
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput><command>lpadmin</command> <option>-p</option> "
"<parameter>danka_infotec_P320</parameter> <option>-o</option> <parameter>job-"
"quota-period=604800</parameter></userinput>\n"
"\n"
"<userinput><command>lpadmin</command> <option>-p</option> "
"<parameter>danka_infotec_FullColor</parameter> <option>-o</option> "
"<parameter>job-page-limit=100</parameter></userinput>\n"
"\n"
"<userinput><command>lpadmin</command> <option>-p</option> "
"<parameter>danka_infotec_HiSpeed</parameter> <option>-o</option> "
"<parameter>job-k-limit=1024</parameter></userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: cupsoptions.docbook:227
#, no-c-format
msgid "Related Error Messages"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: cupsoptions.docbook:229
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once a user reaches his quota limit, he'll get a <errortype>client-error-not-"
"possible</errortype> message, if he wants to print."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: cupsoptions.docbook:238
#, no-c-format
msgid "Installing a <quote>raw</quote> printer"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: cupsoptions.docbook:240
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are different ways to define a <quote>raw</quote> printer. One "
"comfortable one is to use the <command>lpadmin</command> command. Just don't "
"define a &PPD; file to be used for that printer and it will be a raw one:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: cupsoptions.docbook:245
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput><command>lpadmin</command> <option>-p</option> "
"<parameter>Raw_Danka_infotec</parameter> <option>-E</option> <option>-v</"
"option> <parameter>lpd://10.160.16.137/PORT1</parameter></userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: cupsoptions.docbook:247
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Raw printer queues are those which don't touch the print file to transform "
"it to a different file format. You need this for example when printing from "
"&Windows; clients via Samba through a &CUPS; server to a <acronym>PCL</"
"acronym> printer: in this case the &Windows; side printer driver would "
"generate the finished print file format for the target printer and filtering "
"it through &CUPS; filters would only harm the purpose. Under certain "
"circumstances (if you want to make sure that the file goes to the printer "
"<quote>unfiltered</quote> by &CUPS;) the <quote><command>lpadmin</command> "
"without a &PPD;</quote> comes in handy."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: cupsoptions.docbook:262
#, no-c-format
msgid "Troubleshooting &CUPS; in &kdeprint;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: cupsoptions.docbook:264
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This section of the &kdeprint; Handbook will live from the readers' "
"feedback. Here is just a small beginning."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: cupsoptions.docbook:268
#, no-c-format
msgid "Error Messages"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: cupsoptions.docbook:273
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"What does the error <errortype>client-error-bad-request</errortype> mean?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: cupsoptions.docbook:277
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The user sent a file to the &CUPS; which the server could not process. You "
"get this also upon sending an <quote>empty</quote> file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: cupsoptions.docbook:285
#, no-c-format
msgid "And <errortype>client-error-not-possible</errortype>?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: cupsoptions.docbook:288
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"User is either not allowed to print to a certain printer or has achieved his "
"quota (based on file size and/or page number)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: cupsoptions.docbook:295
#, no-c-format
msgid "How about <errortype>client-error-not-found</errortype>?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: cupsoptions.docbook:298
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The user tried to access a nonexistent resource on the &CUPS; server, such "
"as trying to print a nonexistent file, or one that you are denied permission "
"to read."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: cupsoptions.docbook:309
#, no-c-format
